Root normal CI on a4395073 hung in the unchanged current-thread test seat_socket::gui_tests::busy_gui_poll_and_locked_cursor_keep_the_session_and_queued_events. Read actual stack sample /Users/feral/Library/Logs/bboxy450-term/input-current-thread-hang-20261029.sample.txt: lines59-62 test calls Logic::shutdown -> pthread_join, lines113-114 bbt-logic waits in Handle::block_on -> idle_command -> CachedParkThread. The new idle timeout depended on the current-thread timer driver that the synchronous join had blocked. This was a product regression introduced by the input optimization.
logic.rs now owns StopSignal{AtomicBool,Notify} in place of its former atomic-only stop flag. A stop request sets the flag and notify_one retains a wake permit; idle_command checks the flag then biased-selects the stop notification before command/timeout. It wakes even when the runtime timer driver is not running, including the flag-check/notification-registration race. Explicit shutdown, Drop, ready-error and readiness-timeout paths all request the signal. Startup timeout still returns on the existing deadline. No LogicClient fields, protocol/version, operator context or timer budget changed.
New regression current_thread_shutdown_and_drop_have_an_external_watchdog launches only its own test-binary child, with a private account/config, no PTYs and a current_thread runtime. Child confirms the worker is in its idle wait, exits Runtime::block_on so the timer driver stops, then synchronously exercises both explicit shutdown and Drop. Parent requires both child markers and successful exit; its independent std-clock10s watchdog kills/reaps only that owned child on failure. stop_before_idle_registration_is_retained covers a stop preceding waiter registration on paused time. The original hanging test and its runtime/deadline remain untouched.
